# Byte-exact files: hash pinning (release.lock) and cross-machine determinism
# depend on identical working-tree bytes everywhere.
* text=auto
*.py text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.lock text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.html text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
# Shell scripts must stay LF: sh and Terminal.app break on CRLF, and the
# .command launchers are double-clicked on macOS where the exec bit (set in
# git, since Windows checkouts cannot preserve it) needs clean bytes.
*.command text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
# The .eml mail fixtures are synthetic headers, read by the stdlib
# parser (line-ending agnostic); pinned so every checkout sees bytes.
*.eml text eol=lf
# Upstream licence texts are byte-pinned: THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md and
# licenses/third-party/README.md publish their sha256 and byte counts,
# so every checkout must see the LF bytes exactly as committed. The
# build copies frontend/public/licenses into the committed spa tree, so
# those copies pin too: a Windows rebuild must match the committed
# bundle byte for byte.
licenses/third-party/*.txt text eol=lf
frontend/public/licenses/*.txt text eol=lf
src/agentdesk/server/static/spa/licenses/*.txt text eol=lf
# The build-compare contract (a fresh vite build must diff clean against
# this tree) needs LF bytes in index.html on every checkout; the generic
# *.html rule missed a dirty blob already in the index, so the path pin.
src/agentdesk/server/static/spa/index.html text eol=lf
# The registry's release trees are digest-pinned (registry/index.json), so
# every checkout must see their bytes exactly as committed. The extension-
# less LICENSE/NOTICE inside the presentation pack fall outside the *.md
# and *.json rules above; without this pin a CRLF-smudging checkout
# breaks the pin (the gate's registry legs fail on that machine alone).
registry/plugins/presentation-starter/LICENSE text eol=lf
registry/plugins/presentation-starter/NOTICE text eol=lf
# Plugin trees are digest-pinned byte-exactly (registry/index.json,
# bundled-catalog.json), and their LICENSE/NOTICE carry no extension, so
# the text=auto default would flip them to CRLF on a Windows checkout
# and break every pin. The generic rule covers future plugin trees; the
# presentation-pack lines above stay for the tree already shipped.
LICENSE text eol=lf
NOTICE text eol=lf
